 "note": "the vertex pieces of the battlement (art round 13), anchored on the vertex at the walkway's floor, as a post (no +16). Corners are named as the cliffs' (outer_<where the vertex sits on the walkway's tile>, inner_<where it sits on the notch tile>) and need the same classification (src/cliffs.js cornerBase, read on the floor of the SAME layer). Each is the 16 x 16 block that turns the corner, in the quadrant opposite the walkway (outer) or in the notch (inner); the straight pictures at its two ends are unchanged, except at an inner corner where the two edges use their `late` / `early` pictures. An `end` piece completes the half merlon beyond a run's free end."
